  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- HFC phase-down strategy development including stakeholder consultations, workshops, need assessments, documents, drafting of strategy;
-Review of legislative and policy measures including gap analysis, recommendations, drafting and adoption of measures;
-Promotion of energy-efficiency including a description of existing energy- efficiency measures, policies and standards, stakeholder consultations, recommendations;
-Capacity building in the refrigeration sector and related to enforcement including training and seminars, development of training curricula, data surveys;
-Communication and outreach plan including awareness seminars, awareness campaign, production and translation of documents.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is the preparation of Turkmenistan&#x2019;s HFC phase-down strategy and Kigali HFC implementation plan (KIP) stage I for the period 2023-2029. KIP stage I is expected to contribute to Turkmenistan&#x2019;s climate protection efforts and national determined contributions.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Carrying out of a survey of HFC consumption (2019-2021) and its sectoral distribution, surveys of enterprises in the manufacturing and servicing sectors, with analysis of the data to estimate the HFC baselines
2. Stakeholder consultation meetings to sensitize stakeholders and new partners on the implementation of the Kigali Amendment and consolidation of technical capacities in the institutions involved in HFC control.
3. Review of international safety standards and regulations for the safe handling of alternative refrigerants for possible adoption at national level.
4. Organizing consultations led by international RAC experts in promoting efficient practices of operation, maintenance and installation in RAC systems.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Achieved.Technical assistance to the NOU Turkmenistan on the establishment of current consumption of high-GWP HFCs and low-GWP alternatives by substance and on establishment of estimate growth patterns in consumption of high-GWP HFCs and low-GWP alternatives by substances; in interpretation of data obtained during the inventory at a minimum for 2019-2021 years and estimate alternatives used by RAC sectors and support in reviewing the historical use data of the carried out by International consultant.
2. Achieved. Several consultation meetings with stakeholders were held and received detailed information about the project components, the essence of each item separately, and the expected results upon completion of all planned activities of the project.
3. Achieved. The existing national and international safety and performance standards applicable to the RAC sector in Turkmenistan, including standards and regulations on the safe handling of alternative refrigerants and on enhancing energy-efficiency were reviewed and compiled by national standards expert. 
4. Postponed to the beginning of the next year.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Receiving of UNEP funds and allocation of the initial budget</narrative>
